  "description": "KUVKOD crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H138 Co2 Dy4 N4 O29. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.367-5.024 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.23-145.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H138Co2Dy4N4O29. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II).",
